t chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (95). Huntington's all-time high is 108\u00b0F, on July 28, 1930.","t_chg":"Huntington's nights have warmed. Its days have warmed since 1986.","p_chg":"Across 123 complete years: Huntington's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.22\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.15 to +0.29), about +2.8\u00b0F since 1898. Huntington's average high shows no clear change: \u22120.01\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.11 to +0.10) that includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.53\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.19 to +0.88) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.50\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.07 to +0.92). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 9 of 12 months. Highs rose in 3 of 12 months; 3 months fell.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Huntington's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.35 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 45.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 2011 (62.44 in); the driest, 1930 (21.73 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 11 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}